ling. Our live harness reported 0 drops in 20 same-turn open+cancel trials, but this package holds no recorded outcome for that witness.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":149},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":1011},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-compositor-test.sh","kind":"test"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: can the cancel write be lost when resultProc is still running a previous answer?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Rapid repeat summon while resultProc is busy\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-menu-select","shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:finishRequest"],"scenario":"omarchy-shell restarted while an omarchy-menu-select caller polls its done file with no later summon"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The fix covers a superseded request only. If Quickshell crashes or `omarchy restart shell` runs while omarchy-menu-select is polling, nothing writes the done file and the unbounded `while [[ ! -e $done_file ]]` loop in bin/omarchy-menu-select spins forever (tracked as known issue KI-MENU-SELECT-POLL-DEADLOCK, still reproducing). Worth stating upstream so reviewers do not read #9056 as closing every orphaned-process path; a bounded wait / peer-liveness check in omarchy-menu-select is the residual fix.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-select","kind":"file","line":93},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Q6ZS","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: a caller still hangs if the shell dies or restarts with a request in flight (pre-existing, not addressed by this PR)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Shell restart with