g, run `omarchy menu summon system`; assert the picker caller exits 1 with empty output and the System menu opens.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":38}],"title":"Route summon over a pending picker"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #9056 (fixes #9057) adds one guard to Menu.qml open(): an in-flight select/input request is answered as cancelled before the next summon replaces it, so a repeated key press no longer leaves an omarchy-menu-select stuck in its done-file poll. Everything else in this mirror (new requirement SW-REQ-260925-XTGG, spec refreshes, test witnesses, proof.yaml, review/ PoC) is our proof-refresh work, not upstream.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Not by recorded evidence in this package. Changed-code coverage counts 0 changed decisions (the QML guard is outside the coverage basis) and the tests verifying XTGG have no observed outcome at this revision. Change effects were not analyzed for QML/bash.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Can the cancel write be dropped while resultProc is still busy? Should a plain menu summon also cancel a pending picker? Do all callers handle the superseded exit like Escape? The shell-restart hang (KI-MENU-SELECT-POLL-DEADLOCK) remains and is outside this PR.\n\n**Traceability.** 34 requirements touched; the guard is traced to XTGG. Four unmapped-code candidates are our additions: three test helpers (noise) and a PoC script unrelated to #9056 (scope_split).\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** Readiness is blocked (introduced); the next decision is a human judgement on 2 protection reductions, by a policy approver under the approved policy @ ce925cb1edf4. The policy_weakened disclosure and the 5 newly failing gates (incl. the one error, spec_lint_spec_conformance_review_grounded, from citations in our REVIEW-26) come from our refresh files, not the upstream code; they stay blocking until fixed or signed off. 16 other failing checks are unchanged vs baseline."}
